course: dictionary
lesson: 6908
title: Oxen and more than one
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An ox is one big strong farm animal. Oxen is the word for more than one ox. Oxen were used to pull carts and ploughs, so farmers needed a team of them.
explain: Oxen is a plural noun, which means it names more than one thing. Notice the ending -en. Children has the same ending, and old English already had a plural for children, so the -en is added on top of that.
explain: In history, oxen pulled covered wagons on the Oregon Trail. In stories, you may read about oxen working in the fields. In maths, a yoke of oxen is 2 animals, so a yoke is a pair.
fact: An ox is one animal. Oxen is more than one.
fact: Oxen are big, strong farm animals used to pull carts and ploughs.
fact: «When wolves come, musk oxen form a ring with horns out and calves in the middle.»
fact: The -en ending in oxen is an old plural ending, the same as in children.
fact: A yoke of oxen means two oxen working together.
exercise: What is the singular of oxen? | oxes | oxing | oxon | *ox
exercise: «The wagons were pulled west by oxen on the Oregon Trail.» What did the oxen do? | *Pulled the wagons | Flew over the mountains | Sang songs to the travellers | Swam across the sea
exercise: «Musk oxen form a ring facing outwards, with calves in the middle.» Where are the calves? | *In the middle | Inside the wagon | Far away on the hill | On the outside, facing the wolves
test: «A yoke of oxen is two oxen.» How many oxen are in one yoke? | Ten | *Two | Four | One
test: Which word also makes its plural with -en, like oxen? | dog | cat | *children | fish
exam: «Oxen» is the plural of which word, and what ending does it use? | oxen, with -s | ox, with -es | *ox, with -en | oxes, with -en
